      "reasoning": "Turn 4! I drew Settle the Score - a removal spell that exiles a creature (2BB). Let me think about my options:\n\
\n\
**Current mana:** 3 lands (Plains, Swamp, Swamp) + 1 land drop available (Swamp in hand) = 4 mana if I play the Swamp.\n\
\n\
**Options:**\n\
1. Play Swamp → Cast Basri's Acolyte (2WW) - can't, only 1 Plains\n\
2. Play Swamp → Cast Settle the Score (2BB) to exile Concordia Pegasus - that stops the flying damage, but it's tapped and only a 1/3. Might want to save removal.\n\
3. Cast Ghoulraiser (1BB) - 2/2, returns a Zombie from graveyard (no zombies in graveyard though, so just a body)\n\
4. Cast Liliana's Elite (2B) - currently a 2/2 (1/1 + 1 creature in graveyard)\n\
5. Play Swamp + cast Ghoulraiser or Elite, saving mana for Settle the Score next turn\n\
\n\
I think the best play is: Play Swamp, then cast Settle the Score to exile Concordia Pegasus. That removes their only creature and their only source of damage. With 4 mana (1W + 3B), I can pay 2BB for Settle the Score.\n\
\n\
Wait - actually, let me reconsider. If I play the Swamp, I have PWBB available. Settle the Score costs 2BB, which I can pay with PWBB (Plains covers one of the 2 generic). Yes!\n\
\n\
But is it worth using Settle the Score on a 1/3 flyer? It IS my only source of damage right now. And I don't have any flyers to block it. Let me think about this more carefully. Concordia Pegasus has been pinging me for 1 every turn. If I leave it alive, I take more damage but save my premium removal for a bigger threat.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, I play the Swamp and cast Ghoulraiser (1BB). It's a 2/2 body, and I can attack with Devotee. Next turn I can potentially play Basri's Acolyte if I draw a Plains, or Settle the Score for a bigger threat.\n\
\n\
