      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "WHOA! Ghoulraiser is 10/9 with trample?! Opponent must have cast Enlarge (+7/+7 and trample) on their Steel-Plume Marshal, but wait... Enlarge is in opponent's graveyard. And my Ghoulraiser is 10/9 with trample? That makes no sense... \n\
\n\
Wait, looking more carefully: Steel-Plume Marshal is attacking me (it's in combat attacking Opus Trash). And Ghoulraiser is 10/9 with trample and sick. Did opponent cast Enlarge on their own creature that then... no, Enlarge gives +7/+7 to a target creature. It's in their graveyard.\n\
\n\
Oh I see - opponent used Enlarge on Steel-Plume Marshal (3/3 → 10/10 with trample), but wait the combat shows Steel-Plume Marshal 3/3 tapped attacking. And Ghoulraiser is 10/9... \n\
\n\
Actually wait, I think opponent cast Enlarge on my Ghoulraiser! No, that doesn't make sense either - why would they pump my creature?\n\
\n\
